From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theo Slater <theoslater1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 18:32:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] LibWeb: Keep loading SVG images from requesting frames of
 every image

A task for an SVG image document routes its frame requests to that
document's image. While the document is still loading its image does
not exist yet, so the request went to every SVG image of the page
instead. Loading a page with many SVG images then invalidated every
image once for each image that finished loading: Wikipedia's 206 SVG
images produced about 13,000 invalidations while loading.

Such a document has drawn nothing yet, and its image notifies its
clients once it is created, so suppress its frame requests until then.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Libraries/LibWeb/SVG/SVGDecodedImageData.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Libraries/LibWeb/SVG/SVGDecodedImageData.cpp b/Libraries/LibWeb/SVG/SVGDecodedImageData.cpp
index 71a670c7f65911a99a43cc15c1f304e08f997668..97ce127b283d6fddb5689980076b23774dad3b45 100644
--- a/Libraries/LibWeb/SVG/SVGDecodedImageData.cpp
+++ b/Libraries/LibWeb/SVG/SVGDecodedImageData.cpp
@@ -92,6 +92,11 @@ ScopedSVGImageDocument::ScopedSVGImageDocument(DOM::Document& document, FrameReq
         }
     }
 
+    if (!current_image_data && !m_should_unsuppress_frame_requests) {
+        m_page_client->suppress_frame_requests();
+        m_should_unsuppress_frame_requests = true;
+    }
+
     m_page_client->set_current_svg_image_data(current_image_data);
 
     document.set_browsing_context(m_navigable->active_browsing_context());
